        },
        "IssueList": {
          "description": "The CD-2 object-wrap for a list of issues: `{\"issues\":[…]}` (spine §5.3). Shared by\n[`IssueOutput::Issues`] (multi-id `update` / `create_bulk`) and [`QueryOutput::Issues`]\n(`list`/`ready`/`blocked`/`search`/`stale`), so `structuredContent` is an object, never a bare array.",
          "properties": {
            "issues": {
              "description": "The issues in the result set.",
              "items": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/Issue"
              },
              "type": "array"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "issues"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "IssueType": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "Priority": {
          "description": "Issue priority (spine §1.2): a transparent newtype over `i32`, valid range `0..=4`.\n\nOrdering is numeric, so `CRITICAL < HIGH < MEDIUM < LOW < BACKLOG` — this is the order the\nhybrid ready-sort relies on. `Default` is [`Priority::MEDIUM`]. The wire form is the bare\ninteger (`#[serde(transparent)]`), and `Display` renders `\"P{n}\"`.\n\n# Examples\n\n```\nuse unblock_model::Priority;\nuse std::str::FromStr;\n\nassert_eq!(Priority::default(), Priority::MEDIUM);\nassert_eq!(Priority::CRITICAL.to_string(), \"P0\");\nassert_eq!(Priority::from_str(\"p1\").unwrap(), Priority::HIGH);\nassert!(Priority::from_str(\"P5\").is_err());\nassert!(Priority::CRITICAL < Priority::BACKLOG);\n```",
          "format": "int32",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "Status": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/IdOnly",
          "description": "Quick-create: the minted id only."
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Issue",
          "description": "A single issue (`create` / `show` / `reopen` / `restore`)."
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/IssueList",
          "description": "Multiple issues (multi-id `update`; ALSO `create_bulk` — the N created issues), CD-2\nobject-wrapped as `{\"issues\":[…]}`."
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/CloseOutcome",
          "description": "The `close` outcome (`suggest_next` → `newly_unblocked`, FR-11)."
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/DeletePlanOutput",
          "description": "The resolved delete plan (was the ad-hoc `delete_plan_json`)."
        }
      ],
      "description": "The `issue` tool success union — the 5 success shapes across the 8 actions (spine §5.3, D25).\n\n`#[serde(untagged)]` ⇒ each arm serializes as its inner value directly (wire-identical to the\npre-D25 ad-hoc values). The large arms are boxed to keep `clippy::large_enum_variant` clean.",
      "title": "IssueOutput"
    }
  },
  "claim": {
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "The `claim` tool input (spine §5.2 — EXACT shape).",
